From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: castledking <thecastledking@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 04:37:12 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Optimise villager AI

- PoiCompetitorScan runs for every employed villager on every tick and
  looks at every villager within 48 blocks. Read their job sites without a
  map lookup, and compare the job site before reading health, since that
  is the check that almost always fails. Every check is side-effect free,
  so the outcome is unchanged.
- Sort nearby entities by distances worked out once, rather than twice per
  comparison. Both sorts are stable, so the order is unchanged.
- POI searches look up each column's poi chunk once rather than once per
  section.
- Remove streams from GolemSensor, MobSensor, PlayerSensor, TemptingSensor,
  YieldJobSite and TradeWithVillager, and test the entity type before the
  distance in SetLookAndInteract, following Leaf's patches of the same
  names (https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf).
- Do not set a mob's frozen ticks to the value they already have,
  following Leaf.

